{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824954539,"sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e16ffd001CFG0rXwPDoMXgg","sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","messageID":"msg_0b9e16909001JSxsHJKyePkPLt","type":"tool","id":"call_00_iVvvBuWAZNmUedzsMPZ45024","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/paged.txt","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/petsmart/paged.txt, lines 1-400\n1: ~~~ PAGE 1 ~~~\n2: DEFM14A\n3: ~~~ PAGE 2 ~~~\n4: t1500073-defm14a.htm\n5: DEFINITIVE PROXY STATEMENT\n6: t1500073-defm14a - none - 13.4073406s\n7: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n8: UNITED STATES\n9: SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION\n10: Washington, D.C. 20549\n11: SCHEDULE 14A\n12: Proxy Statement Pursuant to Section 14(a) of the Securities\n13: Exchange Act of 1934\n14: Filed by the Registrant ☒\n15: Filed by a Party other than the Registrant\n16: ☐\n17: Check the appropriate box:\n18: ☐\n19: Preliminary Proxy Statement\n20: ​\n21: ☐\n22: Confidential, for Use of the Commission Only (as permitted by Rule 14a-6(e)(2))\n23: ​\n24: ☒\n25: Definitive Proxy Statement\n26: ​\n27: ☐\n28: Definitive Additional Materials\n29: ​\n30: ☐\n31: Soliciting Material under Rule 14a-12\n32: ​\n33: ​\n34: PetSmart, Inc.\n35: ​\n36: ​\n37: (Name of Registrant as Specified In Its Charter)\n38: ​\n39: ​\n40: ​\n41: ​\n42: ​\n43: (Name of Person(s) Filing Proxy Statement, if other than the Registrant)\n44: ​\n45: Payment of Filing Fee (Check the appropriate box):\n46: ☐\n47: No fee required.\n48: ​\n49: ☐\n50: Fee computed on table below per Exchange Act Rules 14a-6(i)(1) and 0-11.\n51: ​\n52: (1)\n53: Title of each class of securities to which transaction applies:\n54: ​\n55: (2)\n56: Aggregate number of securities to which transaction applies:\n57: ​\n58: (3)\n59: Per unit price or other underlying value of transaction computed pursuant to Exchange Act Rule 0-11 (Set forth the amount on which the filing fee is calculated and state how it was\n60: determined):\n61: ​\n62: (4)\n63: Proposed maximum aggregate value of transaction:\n64: ​\n65: (5)\n66: Total fee paid:\n67: ​\n68: ☒\n69: Fee paid previously with preliminary materials.\n70: ​\n71: ☐\n72: Check box if any part of the fee is offset as provided by Exchange Act Rule 0-11(a)(2) and identify the filing for which the offsetting fee was paid previously. Identify the previous filing\n73: by registration statement number, or the Form or Schedule and the date of its filing.\n74: ​\n75: (1)\n76: Amount Previously Paid:\n77: ​\n78: (2)\n79: Form, Schedule or Registration Statement No.:\n80: ​\n81: (3)\n82: Filing Party:\n83: ​\n84: (4)\n85: Date Filed:\n86: ​\n87: ​\n88: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n89: 19601 North 27th Avenue\n90: Phoenix, Arizona 85027\n91: February 2, 2015​\n92: Dear Stockholder:\n93: You are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of the stockholders of PetSmart, Inc., a Delaware corporation, which we will hold at the Sheraton Crescent Hotel, 2620 W. Dunlap Avenue,\n94: Phoenix, AZ 85021, on March 6, 2015, at 1:00 p.m., local time.\n95: At the special meeting, holders of our common stock, par value $0.0001 per share (“common stock”), will be asked to consider and vote on a proposal to adopt an Agreement and Plan of Merger\n96: (as it may be amended from time to time, the “merger agreement”), dated as of December 14, 2014, by and among the Company, Argos Holdings Inc., a Delaware corporation (“Parent”), and Argos\n97: Merger Sub Inc., a Delaware corporation and wholly owned subsidiary of Parent (“Merger Sub”). Under the merger agreement, Merger Sub will be merged with and into the Company (the “merger”),\n98: and each share of common stock outstanding at the effective time of the merger (other than certain shares as set forth in the merger agreement) will be cancelled and converted into the right\n99: to receive $83.00 in cash (the “merger consideration”). If the merger is completed, the Company will become a subsidiary of Parent, an entity which will be owned by a consortium including\n100: funds advised by BC Partners, Inc., La Caisse de dépôt et placement du Québec, affiliates of GIC Special Investments Pte Ltd, affiliates of StepStone Group LP and Longview Asset Management,\n101: LLC.\n102: The board of directors of the Company (the “board”) unanimously (i) determined that the merger agreement and the merger are advisable and in the best interests of the Company and its\n103: stockholders, (ii) approved the execution, delivery and performance of the merger agreement, and (iii) resolved to recommend the adoption of the merger agreement by the stockholders of the\n104: Company and directed that such matter be submitted for consideration of the stockholders of the Company at the special meeting.\n105: The board unanimously recommends that the stockholders of the Company vote “FOR” the proposal to adopt the merger agreement.\n106: At the special meeting, stockholders will also be asked to vote on (i) an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve specified compensation that may be paid or become payable to the named\n107: executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger and (ii) a proposal to approve the adjournment of the special meeting from time to time, if necessary or appropriate, to\n108: solicit additional proxies if there are insufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the proposal to adopt the merger agreement.\n109:  The board unanimously recommends that the stockholders of the Company vote “FOR” each of these proposals.\n110: The enclosed proxy statement describes the merger agreement, the merger and related agreements and provides specific information concerning the special meeting. In addition, you may obtain\n111: information about us from documents filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission. We urge you to, and you should, read the entire proxy statement carefully, including the annexes and\n112: the documents referred to or incorporated by reference in the proxy statement, as it sets forth the details of the merger agreement and other important information related to the merger.\n113: Your vote is very important. The merger cannot be completed unless holders of a majority of the outstanding shares of common stock vote in favor of the adoption of the merger agreement. If\n114: you fail to vote on the adoption of the merger agreement, the effect will be the same as a vote against the adoption of the merger agreement.\n115: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n116: While stockholders may exercise their right to vote their shares in person, we recognize that many stockholders may not be able to attend the special meeting. Accordingly, we have enclosed a\n117: proxy card that will enable your shares to be voted on the matters to be considered at the special meeting even if you are unable to attend. If you desire your shares to be voted in\n118: accordance with the board’s recommendation, you need only sign, date and return the proxy card in the enclosed postage-paid envelope. Otherwise, please mark the proxy to indicate your voting\n119: instructions; date and sign the proxy card; and return it in the enclosed postage-paid envelope. You also may submit a proxy by using a toll-free telephone number or the Internet. We have\n120: provided instructions on the proxy card for using these convenient services. Submitting a proxy will not prevent you from voting your shares in person if you subsequently choose to attend\n121: the special meeting. Even if you plan to attend the special meeting in person, we request that you complete, sign, date and return the enclosed proxy card and thus ensure that your shares\n122: will be represented at the special meeting if you are unable to attend.\n123: If you hold your shares in “street name” through a broker, bank or other nominee you should follow the directions provided by your broker, bank or other nominee regarding how to instruct\n124: your broker, bank or other nominee to vote your shares. Without those instructions, your shares will not be voted, which will have the same effect as voting against the proposal to adopt the\n125: merger agreement.\n126: If you have any questions or need assistance in voting your shares, please contact our proxy solicitor, Innisfree M&A Incorporated, toll free at 1-877-456-3510\n127: .\n128: Thank you for your continued support.\n129: Very truly yours,\n130: DAVID K. LENHARDT\n131: President and Chief Executive Officer\n132: Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities regulatory agency has approved or disapproved the merger, passed upon the merits or fairness of the merger or passed\n133: upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\n134: This proxy statement is dated February 2, 2015 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about February 2, 2015.\n135: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n136: PETSMART, INC.\n137: 19601 North 27th Avenue\n138: Phoenix, Arizona 85027\n139: NOTICE OF SPECIAL MEETING OF STOCKHOLDERS\n140: To the Stockholders of PetSmart, Inc.:\n141: NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a Special Meeting of the Stockholders of PetSmart, Inc., a Delaware corporation (“PetSmart,” the “Company” or “we”), will be held at the Sheraton Crescent Hotel,\n142: 2620 W. Dunlap Avenue, Phoenix, AZ 85021, on March 6, 2015, at 1:00 p.m, local time for the following purposes:\n143: 1.\n144: to consider and vote on a proposal to adopt the Agreement and Plan of Merger (as it may be amended from time to time, the “merger agreement”), dated as of December 14, 2014, by and among the\n145: Company, Argos Holdings Inc., a Delaware corporation (“Parent”), and Argos Merger Sub Inc., a Delaware corporation and wholly owned subsidiary of Parent;\n146: ​\n147: 2.\n148: to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, specified compensation that may be paid or become payable to the named executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger;\n149: ​\n150: 3.\n151: to approve the adjournment of the special meeting from time to time, if necessary or appropriate, to solicit additional proxies if there are insufficient votes at the time of the special\n152: meeting to approve the proposal to adopt the merger agreement; and\n153: ​\n154: 4.\n155: to act upon other business as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement thereof by or at the direction of the board.\n156: ​\n157: The holders of record of our common stock, par value $0.0001 per share (“common stock”), at the close of business on January 29, 2015, the record date for the special meeting, are entitled\n158: to notice of and to vote at the special meeting or at any adjournment thereof. All stockholders are cordially invited to attend the special meeting in person.\n159: The board of directors of the Company (the “board”) unanimously (i) determined that the merger agreement and the merger are advisable and in the best interests of the Company and its\n160: stockholders, (ii) approved the execution, delivery and performance of the merger agreement, and (iii) resolved to recommend the adoption of the merger agreement by the stockholders of the\n161: Company and directed that such matter be submitted for consideration of the stockholders of the Company at the special meeting.\n162: The board unanimously recommends that the stockholders of the Company vote “FOR” the proposal to adopt the merger agreement, “FOR” the advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve specified\n163: compensation that may be paid or become payable to the named executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger and “FOR” the proposal to adjourn the special meeting from time\n164: to time, if necessary or appropriate, to solicit additional proxies if there are insufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the proposal to adopt the merger agreement.\n165: Your vote is important, regardless of the number of shares of common stock you own. The adoption of the merger agreement by the affirmative vote of holders of a majority of the outstanding\n166: shares of common stock is a condition to the consummation of the merger. The advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve specified compensation that may be paid or become payable to the named\n167: executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger and the proposal to adjourn the special meeting from time to time, if necessary or appropriate, to solicit additional proxies\n168: if there are insufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the proposal to adopt the merger agreement each requires the affirmative vote of holders of a majority of the\n169: shares of common stock present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote thereon.\n170: Even if you plan to attend the special meeting in person, we request that you complete, sign, date and return the enclosed proxy card and thus ensure that your shares of common stock will be\n171: represented at the special meeting if you are unable to attend\n172: .\n173: A failure to vote your shares of common stock or an abstention from voting will have the same effect as a vote against the proposal to adopt the merger agreement.\n174: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n175: You also may submit your proxy by using a toll-free telephone number or the Internet. We have provided instructions on the proxy card for using these convenient services.\n176: If you sign, date and return your proxy card without indicating how you wish to vote, your proxy will be voted in favor of the proposal to adopt the merger agreement, the advisory\n177: (non-binding) proposal to approve specified compensation that may be paid or become payable to the named executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger and the proposal to\n178: adjourn the special meeting from time to time, if necessary or appropriate, to solicit additional proxies if there are insufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the\n179: proposal to adopt the merger agreement. If you fail to vote or submit your proxy, the effect will be that your shares will not be counted for purposes of determining whether a quorum is\n180: present at the special meeting and will have the same effect as a vote against the adoption of the merger agreement, but will not affect the advisory vote to approve specified compensation\n181: that may become payable to the named executive officers of the Company in connection with the merger and the vote regarding the adjournment of the special meeting to solicit additional\n182: proxies, if necessary or appropriate.\n183: Your proxy may be revoked at any time before the vote at the special meeting by following the procedures outlined in the accompanying proxy statement.\n184: BY ORDER OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS\n185: PAULETTE DODSON\n186: Senior Vice President, General Counsel and Secretary\n187: Dated February 2, 2015\n188: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n189: ​\n190: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n191: ​\n192: ​\n193: ​\n194: Page\n195: ​\n196: SUMMARY\n197: ​\n198: ​\n199: ​\n200: ​\n201: 1\n202: ​\n203: ​\n204: QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE SPECIAL MEETING AND THE MERGER\n205: ​\n206: ​\n207: ​\n208: ​\n209: 10\n210: ​\n211: ​\n212: CAUTIONARY STATEMENT CONCERNING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n213: ​\n214: ​\n215: ​\n216: ​\n217: 15\n218: ​\n219: ​\n220: THE PARTIES TO THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n221: ​\n222: ​\n223: ​\n224: ​\n225: 16\n226: ​\n227: ​\n228: PetSmart, Inc.\n229: ​\n230: ​\n231: ​\n232: ​\n233: 16\n234: ​\n235: ​\n236: Argos Holdings, Inc. and Argos Merger Sub\n237: ​\n238: ​\n239: ​\n240: ​\n241: 16\n242: ​\n243: ​\n244: THE SPECIAL MEETING\n245: ​\n246: ​\n247: ​\n248: ​\n249: 17\n250: ​\n251: ​\n252: Date, Time and Place of the Special Meeting\n253: ​\n254: ​\n255: ​\n256: ​\n257: 17\n258: ​\n259: ​\n260: Purpose of the Special Meeting\n261: ​\n262: ​\n263: ​\n264: ​\n265: 17\n266: ​\n267: ​\n268: Recommendation