{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825417557,"sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e86cf3001erovylNcAlHc93","sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","messageID":"msg_0b9e1a996001Mu5Rucfj3Zmd1F","type":"tool","id":"call_00_uq9UiYfPWERopgSTJFdQ9556","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\n\nfull = open('full_text.txt').read()\nlines = full.split('\\n')\n\n# page markers (ascending standalone ints)\nprev = 0\nmarkers = {}\nfor i, ln in enumerate(lines):\n    s = ln.strip()\n    if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{1,3}', s):\n        n = int(s)\n        if n == prev + 1 and n >= 1:\n            markers[n] = i\n            prev = n\n\ndef page_of(pos):\n    # pos is character offset in full\n    # find line index by counting\n    line_no = full.count('\\n', 0, pos)\n    pg = 1\n    for n, idx in sorted(markers.items()):\n        if idx >= line_no:\n            pg = n\n            break\n    return pg\n\n# normalized text for searching: also build offset map\nnorm = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', full)\n\nquotes = [\n \"determined to explore more intensively potential changes to the Company’s capital structure, with a focus on returning capital to stockholders\",\n \"the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor\",\n \"JANA Partners filed a Schedule 13D with the SEC disclosing that JANA had acquired 9.9% of the Company’s outstanding common stock\",\n \"Longview made public a letter to the board in which Longview stated that the board should consider the a sale of the Company\",\n \"In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor\",\n \"if the Company were to pursue strategic alternatives, Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the conversations that had taken place in the Spring\",\n \"the board (1) determined to explore strategic alternatives (including a possible sale of the Company) for the Company to maximize value for stockholders\",\n \"including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants\",\n \"24 financial participants (including potential lead buyers as well as large suppliers of equity capital to lead buyers)\",\n \"the Company issued a press release announcing that it determined to explore strategic alternatives for the Company to maximize value for stockholders, including a possible sale of the Company\",\n \"the ad hoc committee directed J.P. Morgan to communicate to Industry Participant the board’s concerns as a result of which Industry Participant would not be invited to participate in the exploratory process\",\n \"Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process, but that if Industry Participant were to wish to submit a proposal or other communication to the Company, the board would consider it\",\n \"In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers\",\n \"all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management presentations involving the Company’s senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business plan information\",\n \"the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014\",\n \"Longview had informed the Company that it would be willing to “roll-over” up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview\",\n \"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest\",\n \"the Buyer Group, which indicated a range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share\",\n \"another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share\",\n \"another bidder (which we refer to as “Bidder 2”), which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\",\n \"From October 30 to November 2, 2014, representatives of J.P. Morgan spoke by telephone with all of the potentially interested parties, including those that did not submit an indication of interest\",\n \"increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share\",\n \"the board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round\",\n \"representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at price levels above their respective initial indications\",\n \"After deliberation and consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together\",\n \"representatives of J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the Company’s fiscal year 2014 financial projections\",\n \"The board had initially targeted Monday, December 15 for completion of the sale process, and had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids\",\n \"the Company set the evening of Wednesday, December 10 (five days, rather than 10 days prior to the anticipated December 15 completion date) as the deadline for submission of final bids\",\n \"the Buyer Group and Bidder 2 submitted their respective comments on the draft merger agreement and other transaction documents, and the Buyer Group provided its financing commitment documents\",\n \"J.P. Morgan arranged introductory meetings between Longview and the Buyer Group, and between Longview and Bidder 2\",\n \"PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2\",\n \"The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash\",\n \"Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash\",\n \"Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share\",\n \"the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014\",\n \"later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price\",\n \"each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents\",\n \"Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash\",\n \"The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash, but stated that it was working to increase the offer within the next few hours\",\n \"the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash\",\n \"the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders\",\n \"On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements\",\n \"the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction\",\n \"ultimately negotiated with the Buyer Group as well as two other bidding groups, neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50\",\n \"the board also established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee (the “ad hoc committee”)\",\n]\n\nok = True\nfor q in quotes:\n    qn = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', q).strip()\n    idx = norm.find(qn)\n    if idx == -1:\n        ok = False\n        print(\"NOT FOUND:\", qn[:90])\n    else:\n        # page: map normalized idx back to original char offset (approx by walking)\n        # simpler: rebuild normalized with mapping\n        pass\nprint(\"all found\" if ok else \