{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825666089,"sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9ec48ad001g1xWopA9UO5DYx","sessionID":"ses_f461f6897ffeZJz46cQwZkb8iB","messageID":"msg_0b9ec4116001dbIWwA5xLcKseE","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_Zogjt6zlw4V5AUjtet530640","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 build_ledger.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\nws3=wb['Questions']\nfor r in range(2,ws3.max_row+1):\n    vals=[ws3.cell(r,c).value or '' for c in range(2,7)]\n    print(ws3.cell(r,1).value, \"total words:\", sum(len(v.split()) for v in vals))\nprint()\nfor r in range(2,ws3.max_row+1):\n    print(\"Q:\", ws3.cell(r,2).value)\n    print(\"  A:\", ws3.cell(r,3).value)\n    print(\"  Why:\", ws3.cell(r,4).value, \"| Rows:\", ws3.cell(r,5).value)\n    print(\"  If diff:\", ws3.cell(r,6).value)\nEOF"},"output":"saved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx\nledger rows: 45\nQ1 total words: 87\nQ2 total words: 74\nQ3 total words: 74\nQ4 total words: 83\nQ5 total words: 64\n\nQ: Round map: one process; Round 1 opened by the first-week-of-October NDA wave, not the earlier contacts; Round 2 opened 11/03 as the final round; the 12/12 call an extension?\n  A: Yes. No target outreach wave is reported, so Round 1 opens at the NDA wave; 11/03 opens the final round; C11 makes 12/12 a Deadline revised.\n  Why: pp. 23–26 (“was contacted by 27 potential participants,” p. 23). | Rows: #8, #9, #13.\n  If diff: If Round 1 opened at the first substantive contacts (late September/early October), #8–#9 become Round 1 and “Opened” shifts.\nQ: Round 1 deadline outcome: Enforced, or Late bids accepted because Bidder 2 raised its indication during the 10/30–11/02 calls?\n  A: Enforced — Bidder 2's raise is dated from 10/30 (not after), and the board selected on 11/03 on the bids in hand.\n  Why: “On October 30, six…” and “From October 30 to November 2…,” p. 24. | Rows: #17, #23 (and Rounds Round 1).\n  If diff: If Late bids accepted: Round 1's outcome label changes; #23's Date from becomes 10/31.\nQ: Round 2 outcomes: 12/05 superseded before arrival (no outcome), 12/10 Extended, 12/12 Enforced — or should 12/05 count as Extended and 12/10 as Enforced?\n  A: As recorded. 12/05 was revised on 12/04–12/05 before arriving, so it has no outcome; 12/10 reached and extended to 12/12; 12/12 reached, then signing.\n  Why: pp. 24–26; improvement request p. 25. | Rows: #28, #29, #36 (and Rounds Round 2).\n  If diff: Counting 12/05 gives “Extended; Extended; Enforced”; treating 12/10 as Enforced gives “Enforced; Enforced.”\nQ: Six parties submitted indications of interest (p. 24), but the Reasons section counts “first round indications of interest from 5 bidder groups” (p. 27). Six or five?\n  A: Six; the narrative says six and the arithmetic reconciles (15 − 6 = 9 non-submitters; 6 − 4 = 2 eliminated). “Five” may count only priced groups.\n  Why: pp. 24, 27. | Rows: #17, #21, #22 (and Rounds Round 1).\n  If diff: If five: residual cohort #21 becomes 2, non-submitter exit #22 becomes 10, and Round 1 “Bids received” becomes 5.\nQ: Bidder 3's 12/10 statement — valuation “would not be above” ~$78, no written offer: bid or valuation statement?\n  A: Not a Bid (C12): a valuation statement without an offer, recorded in its exit row; it “did not submit a written offer.”\n  Why: p. 25. | Rows: #35 (and Rounds Round 2).\n  If diff: If a Bid: add a Bid row with Price high ≈$78.00 and change Round 2 “Bids received.”\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"saved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx\nledger rows: 45\nQ1 total words: 87\nQ2 total words: 74\nQ3 total words: 74\nQ4 total words: 83\nQ5 total words: 64\n\nQ: Round map: one process; Round 1 opened by the first-week-of-October NDA wave, not the earli